        "original_id": "1245b2b2-6d98-5970-9444-aaa9ba958021",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Rousillon Rupes, Titania\n- People: William Shakespeare, Bertram count of Rousillon\n- Works: All's Well That Ends Well, Measure for Measure, Troilus and Cressida, First Folio\n- Spacecraft: Voyager 2\n- Concepts: Shakespearean problem play\n\nFacts:\n- William Shakespeare wrote All's Well That Ends Well between 1604 and 1605.\n- First Folio originally published All's Well That Ends Well in 1623.\n- In Shakespeare studies, All's Well That Ends Well is one of three Shakespearean problem plays alongside Measure for Measure and Troilus and Cressida.\n- Rousillon Rupes is a scarp on the surface of Titania.\n- Rousillon Rupes was named after Bertram, count of Rousillon, a character in All's Well That Ends Well.\n- Voyager 2 first imaged Rousillon Rupes in January 1986.",
